{comment}
  The CONTENT of a plain page, drawn inside the frame (decided 2026-10-20). Overrides the platform's
  renderer of the same name. The revision date shows under every page except one drawn in the bare frame (a landing
  shows its text and nothing else); frame.template is the frame drawing the page, given by the renderer. Each tag
  stands on a line of its own, which the engine drops whole, so every other page renders byte for byte as before.
{endcomment}
<article class="py-2">
  <h1>{var:page.title}</h1>
  <div class="page-content">
    {var:page.body raw}
  </div>
  {if:page.revisedAt}
  {unless:frame.template=`frames/bare.html.dtmpl`}
    <p class="text-secondary small mt-4">Last updated <time datetime="{var:page.revisedAt}">{var:page.revisedAt}</time></p>
  {endunless}
  {endif}
</article>
